# Docker build context for deploy/docker/Dockerfile.dms (context = repo root).
#
# Keep the "web" stage hermetic: it runs `npm ci` from frontend/package.json +
# frontend/package-lock.json, THEN `COPY frontend/ /web/`. If the host's
# frontend/node_modules (or build output) is present in the build context, that
# COPY overwrites the clean npm-ci install with whatever happens to be on the
# host -- non-hermetic, and breaks on any host whose native deps don't match
# linux/x64 (e.g. building on macOS/arm64). Excluding node_modules/dist here is
# what makes the multi-stage split actually mean something.
#
# Do NOT exclude anything Dockerfile.dms COPYs: pyproject.toml, src/, deploy/k8s, or
# frontend/ (package.json, package-lock.json, index.html, src/, vite/tailwind/
# tsconfig configs) -- those must remain in the build context.

# --- Node / frontend build artifacts (must not shadow a clean `npm ci`) ---
**/node_modules
frontend/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Python build/test artifacts ---
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
**/*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
.venv
venv
tests

# --- VCS / worktree metadata ---
.git

# --- Design-reference-only tree; never needed in the image ---

# --- Agent/tooling scratch state, not part of the app ---
.claude
.superpowers

# --- Misc scratch dropped in repo root during manual testing ---
*.png
*.jpeg
